<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 55,623 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 55,623 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 55,623 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday, compared to 75,170 tonnes on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Friday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			41,964	    59,135</p>
<p>    Import cargo			13,659	    16,035</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships are expected to sail and nine to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,600	Wawasan Courage	 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		  6,200	Wawasan Megah	   due</p>
<p>High speed disel    787,750	Chesa Peak City	 26/4</p>
<p>Chemical		 10,000	San Mateo		 26/4</p>
<p>General cargo	   7,702	Ivan legubanski	 26/4</p>
<p>Rock phosphate	 22,000	Artemis II		26/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
